            <ArticleTitle>Management of pain in intensive care settings.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>371-86</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An organized treatment plan for providing analgesia in ICU settings can make a significant difference in patient comfort and outcome. Advanced analgesic techniques are available for use at each level of the &quot;pain pathway.&quot; These include agents and methods that act at the periphery, at the spinal cord level, and through a systemic approach. Consultation with specialists in pain management can help achieve optimum therapy for patients in the ICU setting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
